          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Origins of Zionism</strong><br>\nZionism emerged in the late 19th century as a reaction to widespread discrimination and persecution of Jews in Europe. Theodor Herzl, an Austro-Hungarian journalist, is considered one of the founding fathers of Zionism. He wrote the book \"The Jewish State,\" in which he proposed the creation of a separate state for the Jewish people as a solution to anti-Semitism.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Main Goals of Zionism</strong><br>\nThe main goals of Zionism were the restoration of Jewish sovereignty and the creation of a homeland for Jews in Palestine. By establishing such a state, the Zionists aimed to promote the national and cultural renaissance of the Jewish people, while simultaneously providing a refuge from anti-Semitism.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Balfour Declaration</strong><br>\nA significant step toward the realization of Zionist goals was the Balfour Declaration of 1917. British Foreign Minister Arthur Balfour declared his government's support for the creation of a \"national home for the Jewish people\" in Palestine.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
