          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>UN Partition Plan</strong><br>\nIn 1947, the United Nations proposed a partition plan that called for the establishment of a Jewish and an Arab state in Palestine. The Jewish community accepted the plan, while the Arab side rejected it. The following year, the State of Israel was proclaimed.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Wars and Conflicts</strong><br>\nSince its founding, Israel has been involved in a series of wars and conflicts, mostly with its Arab neighbors. These wars led to significant territorial changes and influenced relations between Israel and the Palestinians, as well as other Arab states.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Oslo Accords</strong><br>\nIn the 1990s, the Oslo Accords were signed between Israel and the Palestinian Liberation Organization (PLO) under Norwegian mediation. These accords led to partial self-governance of the Palestinian territories and laid the foundation for further peace negotiations.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
