            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Settlement Policy</strong><br>\nA central point of the Israeli-Palestinian conflict is Israel's settlement policy in the occupied territories. The settlements are largely considered illegal internationally, and their existence and expansion are main points of contention in the negotiations.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Gaza Strip and West Bank</strong><br>\nThe Gaza Strip and the West Bank are two areas at the center of the Israeli-Palestinian conflict. Both areas have different political and societal conditions, making the conflict complex and difficult to resolve.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Current Developments</strong><br>\nIn recent years, there have been some positive developments in the Middle East, including the normalization of relations between Israel and some Arab states. Nevertheless, the Israeli-Palestinian conflict remains a major challenge and a source of tension in the region.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
